<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Corner mask for the details-page backdrop/trailer card.

     The trailer's TextureView does not follow result_top_holder's outline
     clipping on older GPUs (API 27 era), so a playing trailer renders with
     square corners even though the static backdrop (a normal ImageView)
     is clipped correctly. Instead of relying on clipping, this drawable
     PAINTS the page background colour over everything outside the card's
     24dp rounded corner arc.

     How a shape stroke actually paints (calibrated against two on-device
     builds, pixel-measured): the stroke is laid INSIDE the shape's
     outline, extending inward by its full width; the corner radius is
     the OUTER edge's radius. So for a mask view that is the card rect
     outset by O, with shape radius R and stroke width W:
       - arc centre of the shape = card corner + (R - O) — must equal the
         card's arc centre, i.e. R = 24 + O;
       - inner edge radius = R - W — must equal the card's 24dp arc;
       - paint inside the card along the straight edges = W - O — must
         be 0, i.e. W = O.
     Phase 7.5 FIX-3 (item outset 10dp via layer insets, R 34, W 20)
     satisfied the first two and left W - O = 10dp of paint inside the
     straight edges — measured on device as a 9-9.5dp page-coloured
     inset, which the user accepted (Dracula theme, subtle).

     Phase 8.5B geometry (R 36 / W 24, mask view outset by -12dp margins)
     REGRESSED this: measured on the user's AMOLED screenshot, the
     -12dp margins on the match_parent mask view delivered only ~3dp of
     real outset, so the stroke painted W - O = ~21.5dp INSIDE the card's
     straight edges (photo inset 43px per side, vs 18px in Phase 8) — a
     thick black frame around the thumbnail. Its document also wrongly
     assumed the stroke is centred on the outline.

     Phase 8.6 geometry: the outset is structural, not margin-based.
     result_top_card_frame carries a +20dp positive margin inside
     result_top_card_wrap, and this mask is a plain match_parent child of
     the wrap, so the view's bounds are the card rect outset by a
     guaranteed O = 20dp on every side. With R = 44dp (= 24 + 20, arc
     centre coincides with the card's) and W = 20dp (= O):
       - inner edge radius = 44 - 20 = 24dp: lands exactly on the card's
         corner arc — within the card, the paint covers precisely the
         four corner squares outside the arc, nothing else;
       - straight edges: the band runs from the card's edge OUTWARD
         (20dp of page colour outside the card), so the image again
         fills the card edge-to-edge with NO border, in the backdrop
         and trailer states alike;
       - exterior corner coverage: the band reaches radius 44dp from
         the arc centre, which covers the measured "ear" zone (backdrop
         pixels escaping the holder's clip up to ~10dp above the card's
         top corners, farthest point ~41.6dp from the arc centre) with
         ~2.4dp to spare — the 8.5B ear fix is preserved.
     The stroke colour is the same attr that result_root and the scroll
     content paint behind the card (?attr/primaryBlackBackground) in
     every theme variant, so all exterior paint is invisible by
     construction. -->
<layer-list xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <item>
        <shape android:shape="rectangle">
            <corners android:radius="44dp" />
            <solid android:color="@android:color/transparent" />
            <stroke
                android:width="20dp"
                android:color="?attr/primaryBlackBackground" />
        </shape>
    </item>
</layer-list>
